[[15958,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[15961,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[15964,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[15967,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[15970,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[15973,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[15976,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[15982,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[15988,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[16000,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[17326,"[[geometrycreationandimport.pdf]]"],[309,"[[gps.epub]]"],[504,"[[gps.epub]]"],[1404,"[[gps.epub]]"],[1653,"[[gps.epub]]"],[3189,"[[gps.epub]]"],[3602,"[[gps.epub]]"],[3893,"[[gps.epub]]"],[4109,"[[gps.epub]]"],[4112,"[[gps.epub]]"],[4778,"[[gps.epub]]"],[5042,"[[gps.epub]]"],[5048,"[[gps.epub]]"],[5165,"[[gps.epub]]"],[5183,"[[gps.epub]]"],[5324,"[[gps.epub]]"],[5927,"[[gps.epub]]"],[6269,"[[gps.epub]]"],[6491,"[[gps.epub]]"],[6992,"[[gps.epub]]"],[7427,"[[gps.epub]]"],[7661,"[[gps.epub]]"],[8654,"[[gps.epub]]"],[9376,"[[gps.epub]]"],[9715,"[[gps.epub]]"],[10135,"[[gps.epub]]"],[10138,"[[gps.epub]]"],[10183,"[[gps.epub]]"],[10954,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11209,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11212,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11215,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11218,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11221,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11224,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11227,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11230,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11233,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11236,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11239,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11242,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11245,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11248,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11251,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11254,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11257,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11260,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11263,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11266,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11269,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11275,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11302,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11305,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11311,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11317,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11422,"[[gps.epub]]"],[11893,"[[gps.epub]]"],[12163,"[[gps.epub]]"],[12985,"[[gps.epub]]"],[13141,"[[gps.epub]]"],[13549,"[[gps.epub]]"],[13624,"[[gps.epub]]"],[13972,"[[gps.epub]]"],[16972,"[[gps.epub]]"],[18757,"[[gps.epub]]"],[19165,"[[gps.epub]]"],[20026,"[[gps.epub]]"],[21498,"[[Graded Algebra and Hilbert Theory]] decomposes rings and modules into homogeneous degree pieces. Homogeneous ideals and maps respect those pieces, while degree shifts reposition them without changing their algebraic relationships. Graded localization preserves degree information, and the graded form of Nakayama's lemma identifies minimal homogeneous generators.\n\nA filtration instead records nested approximation levels. Its associated graded ring separates successive layers, while the Rees algebra stores every power of an ideal in one graded object. The Artin-Rees lemma controls how an ideal-power filtration meets a submodule, and Krull's intersection theorem describes what survives every power. Hilbert functions and series count graded pieces; eventual polynomial behavior connects this growth to dimension and multiplicity.\n\n[[Regular Sequences and Syzygies]] studies equations whose successive elements remain non-zero-divisors. Systems of parameters reduce a local module to finite length, while regular systems of parameters characterize regular local rings. Complete intersections are generated by regular sequences of the expected length. Quasi-regular sequences capture a related condition through the associated graded structure.\n\nSyzygies are relations among generators. A presentation matrix records first syzygies, and a free resolution continues by finding relations among relations. Minimal graded resolutions expose graded Betti numbers and projective dimension. Hilbert's syzygy theorem bounds the length of a graded free resolution over a polynomial ring, and Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity summarizes how far generator and relation degrees extend beyond their homological positions."],[20750,"[[Gravitation and Relativity]] moves from Newtonian action at a distance to spacetime geometry. [[Newton's Law of Universal Gravitation]] gives an inverse-square attraction, [[Gravitational Field Strength]] gives force per unit mass, and [[Gravitational Potential]] gives energy per unit mass. [[Escape Velocity]] and [[Orbital Motion]] follow from energy and centripetal requirements. The [[Equivalence Principle]] connects gravity with acceleration, and [[Gravitational Time Dilation]] shows that clock rate depends on gravitational potential.\n\n[[Special Relativity]] preserves the laws of physics and light speed across inertial frames by making measured space and time frame-dependent. [[Time Dilation]] changes elapsed time between frames, and [[Length Contraction]] changes dimensions parallel to relative motion. Both effects preserve a common spacetime interval rather than representing mechanical distortions of matter.\n\n[[Atomic and Nuclear Physics]] probes matter below the atomic scale. [[Rutherford Scattering]] locates atomic mass and positive charge in a compact nucleus. [[Ionizing Radiation]], [[Radioactive Decay]], and [[Half-Life]] describe spontaneous nuclear emissions statistically. [[Nuclear Binding Energy]] connects mass defect to stability; [[Nuclear Fission]] and [[Nuclear Fusion]] release energy by moving nuclei toward greater binding per nucleon. At a deeper level, [[Lepton]]s and [[Quark]]s supply the matter content organized by the [[Standard Model]].\n\n[[Quantum Physics and Cosmology]] begins where classical predictions fail. [[Blackbody Radiation]] motivates quantized energy, and the [[Photoelectric Effect]] reveals photons. The [[de Broglie Wavelength]] assigns wave behavior to matter, confirmed by [[Electron Diffraction]], while [[Wave-Particle Duality]] prevents either classical picture from standing alone. The [[Schrodinger Equation]] evolves probability amplitudes, the [[Bohr Model]] anticipates discrete atomic energies, and the [[Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle]] limits simultaneous spreads of conjugate quantities. On cosmic scales, [[Hubble's Law]] reveals expansion and [[Big Bang Evidence]] connects that expansion with a hot early universe."],[54,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[648,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[1410,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[2697,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[2700,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[2703,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[3174,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[3713,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[3728,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4031,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4652,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4820,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4823,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4826,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4829,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4832,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4835,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[4838,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[5276,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[5687,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[5825,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[8015,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[9205,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[9454,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[9673,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[9676,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[9721,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[10627,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[10765,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[11200,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[11965,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[11971,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[11980,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[12016,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[12367,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[12526,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[12949,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]"],[13636,"[[hands-ondesignpatternswith